{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Divination</b> — it lacks the comparative prefix; [it is] קוסם קסמים (one who divines divinations), that is, one who issues decrees. And קסם is a general term, for the decree of the judgment of the stars. And likewise גזרין that one decrees to be so, that is to say: just as קסם is a decreed thing, so it is fitting that it be upon the lips of a king, that he decree with the judgment of truth and not violate the utterances of his mouth."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:08.331755181Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}